{
  "id": "E01",
  "title": "Spatial domain detection on human DLPFC (12 Visium sections, 3 donors)",
  "question": "How accurately do NeuroSTIAS domains recover manually annotated cortical layers compared with published spatial-domain methods and the 3D-STIAS V4.4.1 approach?",
  "data_origin": "real",
  "baseline_status": {
    "banksy": {
      "status": "ran",
      "detail": ""
    },
    "spagcn": {
      "status": "ran",
      "detail": ""
    },
    "graphst": {
      "status": "ran",
      "detail": ""
    }
  },
  "notes": [
    "Scores exclude spots without a manual layer label (NA).",
    "k (number of domains) is set to the number of annotated layers per section for every method; this is the standard DLPFC benchmark protocol and favours no method.",
    "No histology images were used by any method (SpaGCN run with histology=False).",
    "neurostias (default) uses fixed a-priori parameters; neurostias_lodo selects parameters on the other donors only, so its held-out scores are not optimistically biased.",
    "Published DLPFC ARIs for BANKSY, GraphST and SpaGCN are often higher because they use R mclust clustering and/or histology; here all methods ran on CPU without histology, with Leiden resolution search (BANKSY, GraphST) or k-means initialisation (SpaGCN), so absolute values are not comparable with those papers."
  ],
